# Files excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore for host dev artifacts (`.venv/`,
# `.pytest_cache/`, `.coverage`, `*.egg-info/`) that MUST NOT leak
# into the `alma-audit-dev:latest` image at build time, and into
# the `/tmp/alma_audit_work` copy inside the container at run time
# via the bind-mounted `/src` (`deploy/Dockerfile.dev` runs
# `cp -a /src /tmp/alma_audit_work` from a bind mount, so the
# build context affects both phases).
#
# Concrete incident (AISO-214 review, 2026-08-24): a host
# `.venv/bin/python` symlinked to the host's `/usr/bin/python3`
# gets copied into the container, where `/usr/bin/python3`
# resolves to a *different* interpreter (the container's
# `python3.6`/`python3.11` alternative). The
# `tests/test_exit_codes.py::test_cli_exit_1_on_unreadable_apache_root_via_runuser`
# test prefers `.venv/bin/python` when present, so `nobody` ends
# up running an interpreter that can't `import yaml` and the test
# fails. Excluding `.venv/` here makes the test fall back to
# `sys.executable` (the container's `/usr/bin/python3.11`) which
# has the right site-packages.

# Python build / cache artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
*.egg
build/
dist/

# Virtual environments (host dev artifact — never ship)
.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/
env/

# Test caches
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
coverage.xml

# IDE / editor state
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# alma-audit runtime outputs (operators mount fresh logs at run time)
alma-audit-out/

# VCS + Multica workspace metadata (not needed by the container)
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.multica/
.agent_context/
multica-delegation-*.md
uv.lock
